<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ruleset name="goldberry"
         xmlns="http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset/2.0.0"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://pmd.sourceforge.net/ruleset/2.0.0
                             https://pmd.sourceforge.io/ruleset_2_0_0.xsd"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">

  <description>
    docs/testing.md §2's "blocking after triage" tier, triaged.

    PMD's default rulesets are a style guide with a linter attached: they want
    every field final, every method short, every `if` braced on its own line and
    no comment longer than six lines. This project's comments are prose and its
    painters are long because a rasterizer step is long, so running the defaults
    would produce thousands of findings that are all wrong and one that is not.

    So this is a hand-picked list. Every rule below catches something that is a
    defect in any codebase and is invisible to javac and to Error Prone -- which
    is the only reason to run a third analyser at all. Anything either of those
    already covers is deliberately absent.
  </description>

  <!-- CloseResource is deliberately absent, and it was the first rule tried.
       It found 47 sites and every one was the same false positive: a Window, a
       Popup, a RenderObject or a BackendWindow created in one method, stored,
       and closed later by whatever owns it. That is this toolkit's entire
       lifecycle design (ADR-0043 gives every native handle exactly one owner),
       and PMD cannot model ownership transfer, so the rule reports the pattern
       rather than a leak. A gate that is wrong 47 times out of 47 teaches people
       to skip the report. -->
  <rule ref="category/java/errorprone.xml/UnconditionalIfStatement"/>

  <!-- A caught exception that is neither rethrown, logged nor commented is a
       failure nobody will ever hear about. -->
  <rule ref="category/java/errorprone.xml/EmptyCatchBlock">
    <properties>
      <property name="allowCommentedBlocks" value="true"/>
    </properties>
  </rule>


  <!-- Control flow that cannot do what it looks like it does. -->
  <rule ref="category/java/errorprone.xml/JumbledIncrementer"/>
  <rule ref="category/java/errorprone.xml/MisplacedNullCheck"/>
  <rule ref="category/java/errorprone.xml/BrokenNullCheck"/>
  <rule ref="category/java/errorprone.xml/OverrideBothEqualsAndHashcode"/>

  <!-- A loop that appends to a String is quadratic, and the text stack runs per
       frame. -->
  <rule ref="category/java/performance.xml/StringInstantiation"/>
  <rule ref="category/java/performance.xml/InefficientStringBuffering"/>
</ruleset>
